      "writtenOn": "2026-03-14T15:39:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Yeah, as I pointed in the last patch, we need to check if vcpu-\u003earch.apic before checking the guest_apic_protected flag which is stored in vcpu-\u003earch.apic.\n\nYeah, that was my oversight, sorry for the noise.\n\n\u003e I may rework this patch by enabling the kvm_set_cr8 in the vmx_vcpu_reset, to override the TPR as 0x10, so that don\u0027t need this pkvm_vcpu_reset\n\nYeah, seems like a good idea, in particular to keep CR8 consistent with TPR.\n\nAny reason why in `vmx_vcpu_reset()`, not in `kvm_vcpu_reset()`?",
      "parentUuid": "93a6ce1d_fe77e454",
      "revId": "528d3d893f5ab5c4b9bcd50a7639fbabdf6026e6",
