      "writtenOn": "2026-03-16T12:05:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, makes sense.\n\nAlthough, what I was thinking: the semantics of kvm_vcpu_reset()/vmx_vcpu_reset() is to put the vCPU in the architectural reset state, which, I assume, includes CR8 set to 0. So it might be \"semantically cleaner\" to apply this pKVM-specific CR8 setting to 1 after calling kvm_vcpu_reset(), not inside it?\n\n(That\u0027s not a big deal though, I\u0027m fine either way.)\n\nAlso, in your above diff you remove the comment \"The host VMM handles the virtual APIC for the guest.\" but this comment still applies to the npVM case and to the enable_apicv\u003d0 case (given that you still always remove the original `kvm_set_cr8(vcpu, 0)` from the hypervisor code)?\n\nPlus there is also still the same comment in another place in vmx_vcpu_reset():\n```\n        /* The host VMM handles the virtual APIC for the guest. */\n#ifndef __PKVM_HYP__\n        kvm_make_request(KVM_REQ_APIC_PAGE_RELOAD, vcpu);\n#endif\n```",
      "parentUuid": "4e2a0a52_5f9be260",
      "revId": "528d3d893f5ab5c4b9bcd50a7639fbabdf6026e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
