      "writtenOn": "2026-03-16T14:58:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eAlthough, what I was thinking: the semantics of kvm_vcpu_reset()/vmx_vcpu_reset() is to put the vCPU in the architectural reset state, which, I assume, includes CR8 set to 0. So it might be \"semantically cleaner\" to apply this pKVM-specific CR8 setting to 1 after calling kvm_vcpu_reset(), not inside it?\n\nThis seems make more sense. One benefit I can see is that setting TPR to 0x10 is a x86 generic stuff rather than VMX specific, so doing it in pkvm.c is better.\n\n\u003e(That\u0027s not a big deal though, I\u0027m fine either way.)\n\nThen in this case, I would like to keep it as is.",
      "parentUuid": "f05ede7f_f6927b36",
      "revId": "528d3d893f5ab5c4b9bcd50a7639fbabdf6026e6",
